    2: { sharp: "Listen to the rookie making plans. Adorable.", dry: "The rookie has a plan. Cute.", loud: "LISTEN to the rookie making PLANS! That's ADORABLE!", soft: "Listen to the rookie making plans. That's sweet.", odd: "Listen to the rookie making plans. Next comes a whiteboard." },
    3: { sharp: "Let {b} talk. It was a decent idea.", dry: "Let {b} talk.", loud: "Let {b} TALK! It was a DECENT idea!", soft: "Let {b} talk. It was a decent idea.", odd: "Let {b} talk. I liked the diagram." },
